<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">1 March in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">12 events that happened on 1 March, from 1562 to 2005.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/huguenots" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/huguenots.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1562">1562 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">464 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Massacre of Huguenots at Wassy sparks the French Wars of Religion</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Troops escorting the Duke of Guise attacked Protestants worshipping in a barn at Wassy, killing some 50 to 60. The killings set off more than three decades of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-wars-of-religion">religious civil war</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/kingdom-of-france">Kingdom of France</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-wars-of-religion">French Wars of Religion</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1692">1692 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">334 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Salem witch trial examinations begin</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Magistrates questioned Sarah Good, Sarah Osborne and the enslaved woman Tituba in Salem Village, Massachusetts. Accusations spread, and by autumn twenty people had been executed.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1781">1781 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">245 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Articles of Confederation come into force</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maryland">Maryland</a>'s ratification brought into effect the first constitution of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>. The weak confederation lacked powers to tax and was replaced by the Constitution in 1789.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1815">1815 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">211 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Napoleon lands in France after escaping Elba</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> came ashore at Golfe-Juan near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cannes">Cannes</a> with about a thousand men. Troops sent to stop him joined him instead, and he entered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> on 20 March to begin the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hundred-days-reform">Hundred Days</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1836">1836 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">190 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Texas convention assembles at Washington-on-the-Brazos</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Delegates from across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/texas">Texas</a> met in a half-built hall to decide the province's future while the Alamo was under siege. The next day they declared independence from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1872">1872 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">154 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Yellowstone becomes the world's first national park</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ulysses-s-grant">Ulysses S. Grant</a> signed the act setting aside Yellowstone's geysers and canyons 'for the benefit and enjoyment of the people'. The national park idea spread around the world.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1896">1896 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">130 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Ethiopia defeats Italy at the Battle of Adwa</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/menelik-ii">Menelik II</a>'s army routed an Italian invasion force in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a>. The victory forced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> to recognise Ethiopian independence and became a lasting symbol of African resistance.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/ethiopian-empire">Ethiopian Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-adwa">Battle of Adwa</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/menelik-ii">Menelik II</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1896">1896 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">130 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Henri Becquerel discovers radioactivity</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Becquerel found that uranium salts left in a drawer had fogged a photographic plate without any sunlight. He had discovered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/radioactivity">radioactivity</a>, soon investigated by Marie and Pierre Curie.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1919">1919 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">107 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Koreans rise against Japanese rule in the March 1st Movement</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A declaration of independence was read in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seoul">Seoul</a>, and peaceful demonstrations spread across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korea">Korea</a>. Japanese forces suppressed them, killing thousands, but the movement inspired Korean nationalism.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korea">Korea</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1947">1947 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">79 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">International Monetary Fund begins operations</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Created at the Bretton Woods conference of 1944, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/international-monetary-fund">IMF</a> opened for business in Washington. It was designed to stabilise exchange rates and lend to countries in balance-of-payments difficulties.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/international-monetary-fund">International Monetary Fund</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1954">1954 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">72 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Castle Bravo, the largest US nuclear test, contaminates the Pacific</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The hydrogen bomb tested at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bikini-atoll">Bikini Atoll</a> yielded 15 megatons, far more than predicted. Fallout sickened Marshall Islanders and the crew of the Japanese fishing boat Lucky Dragon No. 5.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/2005">2005 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">21 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">US Supreme Court bans the execution of juvenile offenders</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In Roper v. Simmons the Court ruled five to four that executing people for crimes committed under 18 was cruel and unusual punishment. The decision spared some 70 people on death row.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 1 March <span class="n">5</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-vii-of-leon-and-castile"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/alfonso-vii-of-leon-and-castile.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Alfonso VII of León and Castile</span><span class="tp">1105–1157</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/vladislaus-ii-of-hungary"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/vladislaus-ii-of-hungary.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Vladislaus II of Hungary</span><span class="tp">1456–1516</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/john-de-britto"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/john-de-britto.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">John de Britto</span><span class="tp">1647–1693</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/pham-van-dong"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pham-van-dong.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Pham Van Dong</span><span class="tp">1906–2000</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/dalia-grybauskaite"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/dalia-grybauskaite.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Dalia Grybauskaitė</span><span class="tp">b. 1956</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 1 March <span class="n">5</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ayurbarwada-buyantu-khan"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ayurbarwada-buyantu-khan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ayurbarwada Buyantu Khan</span><span class="tp">1285–1320</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/amadeus-vi-count-of-savoy"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/amadeus-vi-count-of-savoy.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Amadeus VI, Count of Savoy</span><span class="tp">1334–1383</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/leopold-ii-holy-roman-emperor"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/leopold-ii-holy-roman-emperor.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Leopold II, Holy Roman Emperor</span><span class="tp">1747–1792</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/gabriele-dannunzio"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/gabriele-dannunzio.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Gabriele D'Annunzio</span><span class="tp">1863–1938</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/mustafa-barzani"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/mustafa-barzani.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Mustafa Barzani</span><span class="tp">1903–1979</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
